    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0b83af766d7fb9328f3f5442b92d2f1744ec67f93097c2e8706bb9f95dba7441",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Within this paper's recipe/correlation comparison, the polynomial length sets a discrete swap cutoff. The signed-set recipe supplies swap cardinality, contour displacement suppresses terms with X<T^{|U|}, and choosing ell by T^ell<=X<T^(ell+1) therefore fixes the deepest swap layer retained and the ell-block refined correlation object used to reproduce it.",
