    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_342f9f14d099255a5142bfab8c91d0e4df698cddc985c9bdbcaf9b086bcce278",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The normalization w_ell aligns two redundant presentations because the same multiplicity (ell!)^2 ell^(2(k-ell)) occurs on both sides: it counts decompositions realizing a fixed ell-swap and routed factor/direction-discrepancy systems representing the same underlying (m,n). Dividing by this common fiber size makes the partition sum and the correlation-system enumeration comparable, including strata with zero discrepancies.",
