      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_40eda213f829e60924d656c5464786893c6eb7619f22b4f47664e45cba1b401e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "After pole selection and the zeta functional equation reorganize the modeled correlation expression, the remaining global comparison localizes prime by prime. At one prime, formal power series encode the Euler factor; minimum-index decomposition collapses the constrained block convolution to the diagonal pairing C, and a three-state inclusion-exclusion over blocks reconstructs the swapped Euler factor.",
