    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8688b79a65ecc4e630140fbd605bd18e4d807835b580349bb9de256ab90d4f18",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Vanishing discrepancies are boundary strata that reduce, rather than erase, the active correlation dimension. Coprimality turns h_j=0 into the exact parametrization m_j=kappa_j M_j and n_j=kappa_j N_j; factoring those blocks rescales the cutoff and leaves only the nonzero-discrepancy blocks for oscillatory analysis, while the inactive blocks remain as diagonal coefficient factors. The hybrid local identity consequently augments shifts only in active blocks, producing lower-cardinality swaps.",
