      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c69cae9e493dd20d94d4973312604bb2d9b98fe085e94a968e7b76a2985bd914",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The correlation-to-swap bridge is staged: convolution exposes paired block ratios, rational directions M_j/N_j with a coupled product constraint separate solution families that a naive delta-method treatment would miss, discrepancies h_j turn those ratios into additive local constraints, and the transformed all-nonzero stratum is then identified with recipe terms selecting one shift from every paired block.",
